id: pm-linear-estimate-unit-provenance
title: Preserve team estimate scales and explicit effort conversions
description: Preserve Linear team estimate scale and declared points-to-effort mapping alongside imported estimates; identify estimates invalidated by a team scale change.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: "gh:unbraind/pm-linear#189","gh:unbraind/pm-linear#191","gh:unbraind/pm-linear#193"
created_at: "2026-10-29T01:53:20.572Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T23:23:52.493Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Five points never become five minutes without a declared conversion; changing one team scale affects only its items; unconvertible estimates remain usable as native points.
comments[91]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T01:53:34.597Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against the installed CLI SDK public declarations, existing Linear estimate tags and round-trip features, and pm-gantt-chart duration inputs. Core estimated_minutes is numeric effort; Gantt consumes minutes and prior capacity work consumes estimates. Neither knows Linear team identity or scale settings. This feature owns provider unit provenance and an explicit scale-bound lookup conversion, preserving native points when unmapped. Existing atomic replay revision follow-up remains relevant; transactions do not exclude ordinary writers (pm-cli#1620)."
  "2026-10-29T02:03:57.444Z",codex-agent,"Implemented versioned per-item unit contracts with exact discrete conversion lookups and bounded team-scoped inspection. Provenance uses lowercase hexadecimal encoding because SDK tag normalization changes letter case; the real SDK tests caught this and the producer/reader now share one codec. Unit-aware writes use a single native mutation per item, registered status roles, explicit scopes and SDK history revision checks. The ordinary-writer read-to-write window remains and is documented; no lock-isolation claim."
  "2026-10-29T02:25:52.769Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public tracker validation passed against main: 112 items, 232 files, 1644154 bytes, 2 complete inspections, unchanged SHA-256, no git executable. No owned unit contracts exist in that corpus; conversion coverage is explicitly synthetic. Targeted network tests exercised sync and both import aliases in serial and transaction modes; the 500-sequence SDK reference-model test uses independent bounded tracker pairs with random custom lifecycle registries, whitespace, native fields, relationships, ambient focus and older-input replays."
  "2026-10-29T02:36:40.912Z",codex-agent,"Acceptance probes passed: five points stay native with no implicit minutes; explicit 5-to-240 lookup; only the changed team invalidates; zero, null and unmapped values remain native. Packed 2026.10.28 host acceptance passed project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx: 35 command assertions, 75 read-only provider requests, zero provider mutations, 571-byte single-item JSON receipts. Behavioral revert in a disposable copy changed only buildItemPlan provenance production: reverted 0 pass/1 fail; unchanged implementation 1 pass/0 fail. Initial linked-test invocation exposed the fixture directory setup error, now fixed. The pinned CLI refuses timeout_seconds metadata under the existing peer floor because it requires guarded item format 2; use runtime --timeout 1800 instead, without changing pins. Linked-test evidence recording is disabled by project policy, so results are retained in this item and validation documents."
  "2026-10-29T02:37:36.564Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and acceptance probes are ready for review. The CI npm and Bun release gates will provide full-suite evidence at the pushed head, with unchanged coverage thresholds; local work uses focused tests, typecheck, docstring lint and diff checks because the shared host is saturated. The 500-sequence test rotates SDK sync, command sync, both importer aliases and host export, compares every touched native field through real SDK reads, and samples exact preview/apply equality. Concurrency guarantees explicitly retain the SDK read-to-write window (pm-cli#1620); provider-less legacy transaction migration remains owned by pm-linear-atomic-replay-revision. The item remains in progress for orchestrator verification and is not closed."
  "2026-10-29T02:48:43.027Z",codex-agent,"The seeded model caught a terminal retry mismatch at sequence 100: the no-op projection omitted close_reason even though the native update writes it. Fixed the projection, preserve an existing native close reason, and use the public PmClient plus loadGuardedRuntimeSchema. Added a focused SDK-oracle regression spanning active, terminal_done and terminal_canceled registries, create and retry; it passes. Full 500-sequence validation remains in both CI release gates. Local focused execution omits that expensive model case on this saturated host; the earlier model probe reached sequence 100 before exposing the repaired defect."
  "2026-10-29T02:56:09.080Z",codex-agent,"Final implementation keeps existing native close reasons, validates supplied CLI guard types and bounded regular input files before reads, and uses the same SDK canonical projection for unchanged decisions. Targeted custom-registry create/retry oracle passes; typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and whitespace checks pass. Full-model and full npm/Bun release evidence will be taken from the PR CI at the final head. All native schema/transaction capabilities are from the pinned supported SDK loaders; no provider or hosted mutations were used for validation."
  "2026-10-29T03:04:50.707Z",codex-agent,"Final focused direct run passed 8/8 with node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-skip-pattern=\"seed 1620\" test/estimate-units.test.ts (80558 ms). The earlier negative-lookahead name filter did not exclude the model in Node, so the linked focused command now uses the explicit skip-pattern flag. The final packed recheck passed all five host layouts again. Complete 500-sequence model validation is retained unchanged in CI; local full-gate execution is intentionally avoided per the shared-host rule. Typecheck, test compilation, docstring lint and diff checks pass."
  "2026-10-29T03:27:19.154Z",codex-agent,"First CI measured 418 tests: 417 passed, including all 500 new unit sequences; an existing ownership property rejected the new enumerable expectedRevision plan property. Moved revisions to an internal map so public/native plans retain their prior shape. Also bind compensation to the SDK producer receipt plus planned body, verified against native history, with per-invocation write nonces; a peer edit before the ownership observation is preserved. Targeted compensation and plan tests passed 2/2. Expanded the seeded model to check native author/type and removed unused test imports flagged by static analysis. No coverage threshold changed; final head requires fresh npm and Bun CI gates."
  "2026-10-29T03:57:10.228Z",codex-agent,"Second CI passed all 419 tests, including the existing ownership 500-sequence model and the new 500-sequence unit model. The unchanged 100 percent function gate exposed one uncalled sort comparator because the new unit tests used single-item batches. Added a real multi-item regression: deterministic target order, reordered replay without duplicates, and one peer-superseded item skipped while its independent peer updates. Targeted coverage located the gap; no threshold or source exclusion changed. DeepScan reports zero new issues at the preceding head."
  "2026-10-29T04:20:26.511Z",codex-agent,"A real SDK adversarial round trip reproduced a namespace collision: source estimate 5 plus a provider label estimate:9 exported estimate 9; source cycle Actual plus label cycle:foreign exported foreign. Fixed literal-label encoding to cover the estimate/cycle namespaces, with versioned records bound to provider identity and producer/validator byte bounds. Older foreign literal tags remain data. Added the collision to the seeded model and a dedicated real-SDK regression, including the maximum documented Unicode label length; focused schema/collision tests passed 2/2. This extends the original native-field round-trip acceptance and does not infer effort."
  "2026-10-29T04:41:56.737Z",codex-agent,"Final source d8bfc4847c4d98f3fa43bdfb5f28da4c10ca1ef6 passed packed acceptance on host 2026.10.28 in project-local, npm-global, Bun-global, npx and bunx: 35 command assertions, 75 read-only provider requests, zero provider mutations, 571-byte single-item JSON receipts. Final artifact SHA-256 b59013a97a408a46641611dc7722d1f575bd42cd0ccd7e8325a1aa51e1e03cb9. Its CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40817266950 remains queued for npm, Bun, Node 22 and Node 26 after 20 minutes; this source head is not certified. Preceding head 2741321 passed https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40815085127 with npm 420/420 and Bun 420/420 tests, each measuring 99.59 percent line, 96.76 percent branch and 100 percent function coverage at unchanged thresholds. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/189 is ready for review. This receipt-only commit requires fresh exact-head CI, which will be reported on the PR; follow the existing 30-minute source-push wait cutoff if runners remain unavailable. Remaining risks are the ordinary-writer final read-to-write window (pm-cli#1620) and the separately tracked legacy provider-less replay path. The item remains in progress and the claim remains released for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T05:09:19.420Z",codex-agent,"Resumed for review round 1. The worktree is clean and current origin/main is already an ancestor, so no merge is needed. The blocking finding is valid and violates previews/plans reuse the apply path and producer/validator agreement: ownership acquisition omits team scale fields, does not pass existing conversion tags into planning, and projects through the legacy writer even when import selects the unit-aware writer. Whole-package search found the two GraphQL issue projections, the ownership projection coordinator, the unit dry-run coordinator, all three import dispatchers, SDK sync, and JSON/TOON ownership output. The supplied review has one blocking finding and no additional non-blocking findings. Plan: share acquisition fields and execute the production import coordinator in isolated ownership projections; add adversarial cross-path tests, packed consumer checks and disposable behavioral reverts, then serial full gates with the existing one-worker coverage configuration."
  "2026-10-29T05:23:53.511Z",codex-agent,"Class fix: one shared GraphQL issue selection now supplies import and ownership, and the isolated ownership projection runs syncLinearIssues itself, selecting the production unit-aware or legacy coordinator and carrying saved conversion tags through the normal planner. The ownership mapping revision changes so old observations require fresh acknowledgement. Focused tests passed 3/3; the linked pm regression passed 1/1 in 108477 ms. It covers 16 combinations of legacy/unit input, SDK/command/import aliases and atomic/ordinary writes, with acknowledged JSON/TOON output and byte-identical source checks. Disposable behavioral reverts independently remove team metadata from ownership acquisition and select the legacy writer inside previewLinearOwnership: each gives 0 pass/1 fail with the expected SDK-read projection mismatch; the unchanged implementation gives 1 pass/0 fail. Evidence is docs/ownership-import-parity-revert.json. The existing 500-sequence model now checks ownership projection against SDK-read applied state after every operation and samples acknowledged replays. Its local run was intentionally interrupted after reaching sequence 100, with no assertion failure, because of the original saturated-host rule; complete model and full npm/Bun release evidence will come from one-worker CI gates. No test, assertion, operation count or threshold was weakened."
  "2026-10-29T05:31:17.768Z",codex-agent,"Final re-review validation before CI: the remaining targeted ownership compatibility suite passed 23/23 (273097 ms), including custom status registries, immutable source isolation, installed host SDK links, malformed/nullable inputs, duplicate baselines, typed dispatcher refusals and literal tag producers. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-skip-pattern=\"500 seeded|ownership shares every\" test/ownership.test.ts. Typecheck, build:test, docstring lint (8 files, 108 declarations) and diff checks pass. The updated single packed artifact passed project-local, npm-global, Bun-global, npx and bunx on host 2026.10.28: 50 command assertions, 105 read-only provider requests, zero provider mutations, 571-byte estimate receipts and 3331-byte ownership receipts with acknowledged unchanged JSON/TOON. Artifact SHA-256 8046e3952531dd890507330338ef1bfc9b80de0cff0057b8567e1cd831bd0925. docs/estimate-packed-validation.json records the digest and counts; docs/ownership-import-parity-revert.json records both failing reverts and the passing fixed regression. Fresh npm and Bun CI release gates at unchanged thresholds remain required; the full 500-sequence model is not claimed as a local pass. CI run URLs and exact-head counts will be recorded on PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/189. No additional non-blocking findings were supplied or found in the PR review comments. Keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T05:50:01.814Z",codex-agent,"CI at 4729b2c exercised 422 tests: npm, Bun and Node 26 each passed 421 and failed the existing ownership 500-sequence model immediately on a custom terminal status. The expanded estimate/import/ownership 500-sequence model passed in all three jobs (104950, 165094 and 174071 ms). A disposable diagnostic exposed the native repeat-close guard: the old projection deliberately forced legacy mutation rows in its owned copy, whereas the production coordinator correctly refuses that real repeat close without force. Restored the copy-only legacy adapter around the actual importLinearAtomic coordinator; production imports and unit-aware writes retain their own policies. Projection journal identity includes SDK target revisions and a separate namespace, preventing copied committed journals from overriding a fresh observation. Added a focused done/canceled custom-role oracle and historical-journal replay case, without weakening the existing 500-sequence test. The new immutable-source test initially included its own SDK get after the baseline snapshot, which records context usage; moved that setup read before the snapshot while retaining the full byte comparison."
  "2026-10-29T06:01:23.462Z",codex-agent,"Final compatibility validation: acquisition, writer-selection and copy-only legacy permission behavioral reverts each fail 0 pass/1 fail; fixed implementation passes both cross-path and custom-terminal/historical-journal tests 2/2. The focused terminal test passed directly 1/1 and through the linked pm runner 1/1 (16221 ms). All five packed host layouts now exercise both scale-aware acknowledged JSON/TOON and the legacy custom-terminal projection: 55 command assertions, 115 read-only provider requests, zero provider mutations, 571-byte estimate receipts and 3331-byte ownership receipts. Final artifact SHA-256 72d2ba9bf55b35e5c8fd9b0439103fb66242a5e3a90bd5606b3c65ef12511ae2; receipt docs/estimate-packed-validation.json. Typecheck, test compilation and docstring gate remain passing, with unchanged thresholds and all existing tests retained. The previous CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40823998199 failed only the old custom-terminal ownership model; its expanded estimate/ownership model passed all 500 sequences in both release gates. Fresh exact-head npm/Bun gates are required after this correction and will be linked on PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/189. Keep this item in progress and release only this agent claim for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-29T06:44:55.902Z",codex-agent,"Resumed for review round 2. The worktree is clean and origin/main remains an ancestor, so no merge is needed. The supplied blocker is valid: target contents from the certified corpus can precede the independently captured history revision, and the missing-revision fallback can silently authorize an unpaired plan. This violates coherent compare-and-set observations and the rule that every expected revision must fence the exact data used for planning. Whole-package search found sync snapshot acquisition, the shared revision helper also used by ownership projection journals, unit dry-run/recovery inspection, every SDK/CLI/import alias, and the readItems test seam. No additional non-blocking findings were supplied. Plan: validate planning images against revision-bracketed native SDK documents using the SDK canonicalizer, refuse missing/incoherent observations per target, retain independent targets, and add SDK-backed boundary/property and packed-consumer evidence plus a disposable revert proof. Full npm/Bun release evidence remains in one-worker CI under the original saturated-host rule."
  "2026-10-29T07:00:22.696Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 class rule: a compare-and-set token must describe the same SDK-canonical document used to plan the mutation; an absent observation cannot authorize a write. The complete linked corpus is now compared with each bracketed SDK document before retaining its history revision. Acquisition changes or missing targets leave no token; inspect, apply and committed-journal reconciliation refuse such targets rather than adopting a newer revision. Package search found this acquisition shared by SDK sync, command/import aliases, atomic dry-run and isolated ownership projection; output handlers already retain bounded skip receipts in JSON and TOON. Provider-less legacy atomic replay remains separately tracked by pm-linear-atomic-replay-revision. Targeted acquisition matrix passed 2/2: 16 peer/ABA cases across four boundaries and both modes, native fields plus relationships preserved via SDK reads, independent targets progress, missing observations/deleted targets skip, stable mappings still apply. Main remains an ancestor (7 commits ahead, 0 behind); no merge required. No additional inline review findings were returned."
  "2026-10-29T07:02:26.327Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node test/revert-estimate-snapshot.ts docs/estimate-snapshot-revert.json exercised two behavioral mutants in disposable non-git copies only. Removing planning-image equality produced 0 pass / 1 fail; restoring missing-revision fallback produced 0 pass / 1 fail. Restored source passed 2 / 2; reviewed checkout was never mutated. The adversarial matrix uses real SDK writes/readback rather than SDK mocks or a handwritten native normalizer. Typecheck of source/tests and docstring gate passed (108 declarations)."
  "2026-10-29T07:09:13.810Z",codex-agent,"Focused linked regression completed successfully: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-skip-pattern=\"seed 1620\" test/estimate-units.test.ts passed 13/13, exit 0. The existing 500-sequence model is reserved for exact-head CI under the saturated-host instruction. The tracker policy intentionally disables persisted test-result records; the run executed through pm test --run --progress --only-last --timeout 600 and its result is retained here. PR comments and reviews contain no further actionable findings; skipped review services do not establish approval. Packed native-process interleaving acceptance remains in progress after one unexpected receipt, which is being diagnosed before recording evidence."
  "2026-10-29T07:15:13.713Z",codex-agent,"Ownership parity regressions also passed 2/2: every writer/alias agrees with acknowledged ownership observations, and isolated custom-terminal projections retain their native SDK behavior. Packed runner diagnosis proved the peer command was refused because --unset does not accept a CSV list; it now emits one flag per scope. Host CLI compact update receipts expose changed_field_count, which the runner verifies before asserting conversion readback. Provider callback exceptions are retained and surfaced instead of being masked by HTTP retry. This corrects test infrastructure only; no product assertion or existing test was weakened."
  "2026-10-29T07:25:53.830Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 local evidence: focused linked unit tests 13/13; ownership regressions 2/2; two behavioral revert mutants each 0/1 and restored source 2/2; source/test typechecks and 108-declaration docstring gate passed. One exact packed artifact passed all five host layouts (project-local, npm-global, Bun-global, npx, bunx) on 2026.10.28: 115 feature assertions, 30 real ordinary-CLI-writer interleavings, 265 read-only provider requests, zero remote mutations; estimate JSON 571 bytes, ownership JSON 3331 bytes. SHA-256 f36e9ca859c99bb0a7ebc03ca937c78fde2e916a9c54b34ab67e3f6b637c1d90. Receipts are linked in docs. Public read-only validation remains 112 items, 232 files, 1644154 bytes, two inspections, unchanged source and 275-byte receipt; this corpus has zero unit contracts, so conversion tests are synthetic real-SDK evidence. No production source changed after the passing regressions. Final npm/Bun release gates and both full 500-sequence models will run in CI with one worker; exact-head URLs/counts will be reported in PR 189. The final SDK read-to-write window remains documented (pm-cli#1620), and the independent provider-less replay follow-up remains open. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-29T07:27:53.128Z",codex-agent,"Pre-push checks: changelog generation/check and git diff --check passed; shipped CHANGELOG bytes were unchanged after final tracker writes, preserving the validated artifact. Default local health refused an ambient pm-github extension requiring host 2026.10.28 while this repository pins 2026.10.24. The same strict health command with --no-extensions passed, including settings, integrity, history drift and required merge-driver checks; existing provenance advisories are retained unchanged. No dependency pin, global extension setting or history record was repaired. Fresh CI will execute the normal project health gate."
  "2026-10-29T08:27:33.171Z",codex-agent,"Round 3: resumed from clean feccb7e, origin/main remains an ancestor (8 ahead, 0 behind), feature item reclaimed. Both blockers reproduce. Rules violated: append-only compensation must remain retryable without treating our own tombstone as foreign; declared host compatibility must cover every SDK function used by default commands. Native probe confirmed create/delete retains two valid history records and PmClient.create refuses the reserved identity. Plan: verify positive package-owned lineage through SDK history, restore the same identity through native SDK with revision checks around every dependent mutation, preserve all audit records and skip foreign/peer-altered tombstones. Search includes creation compensation, recovery/reconciliation, SDK/CLI/import aliases, previews and renderers. Align peer, manifest and docs minimum to the existing tested 2026.10.24 development SDK without changing that pin; certify minimum and current 2026.10.28 packed hosts in all five layouts. Add adversarial history/retry tests, compatibility contract assertions and disposable behavioral reverts; full npm/Bun gates remain in CI under the shared-host rule."
  "2026-10-29T08:52:16.122Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 class audit found two additional instances and fixed them through shared paths: a recovered historical conversion now feeds the ordinary buildItemPlan producer and is paired with its tombstone revision, preventing a peer rollback during planning from authorizing stale tags; scale-aware estimate=ignore imports now retain the same guarded writer instead of bypassing compensation. New SDK boundary matrix covers live peer edits at restore/update/compensation and tombstone ABA via an ordinary non-atomic peer import while the atomic transaction is active. Foreign or malformed deletion records skip alone; the earlier uninterrupted create/delete format remains accepted only with SDK-verified birth, identity and compensation lineage. Runtime host declarations and upgrade remedies now agree on 2026.10.24; the dev pin remains 2026.10.24, and atomic help explicitly states concurrent SDK/CLI writers can interleave. Focused recovery/host tests passed 6/6, separate tombstone ABA test 1/1, and ignore-mode recovery 1/1. Packed validation is expanded to one artifact across minimum/current hosts and all five layouts, with real SDK-generated rollback histories and SDK-normalized export references."
  "2026-10-29T09:24:13.160Z",codex-agent,"Additional class checks: foreign unlinked identities with unreadable native history now skip alone, and all-foreign batches avoid empty transaction journals. Per-target journal reconciliation no longer depends on whether another target already produced a skip. Native SDK creation probes established that valid IDs may exceed the provider ID length limit; rollback receipts now use a bounded native-ID domain, share their byte limit between producer/reader, and preserve those IDs through repeated compensation. SDK-native role tests cover active, blocked and canceled terminal registries and compare status with SDK-produced reference values. The packed reference comparison now keys exports by provider identity, rather than assuming corpus order. Earlier export order assertion failure was test infrastructure; no product assertion was removed. Final source is frozen for fresh packed validation on 2026.10.24 and 2026.10.28 and expanded disposable revert proofs."
  "2026-10-29T09:32:35.826Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node test/revert-estimate-recovery.ts docs/estimate-recovery-revert.json completed nine independent behavioral mutants in disposable copies: retained histories always foreign, first-birth-only compensation, missing restore/update fence, lost historical mapping, adopting a newer tombstone revision, estimate-ignore bypass, unreadable foreign history aborting peers, provider-ID bounds imposed on native IDs, and the unsupported old host floor. Each produced 0 pass / 1 fail; fixed source passed 7/7, and the reviewed checkout was never changed by reverts. The native-ID corpus includes SDK-valid IDs beyond 128 characters and randomly named active/blocked/canceled registries, with SDK-produced status references. Existing provenance, ownership and snapshot regressions remain intact. Packed minimum-host validation has passed project-local, npm-global, Bun-global and npx; bunx and the current-host matrix remain in progress."
  "2026-10-29T09:53:14.377Z",codex-agent,"Final round-3 local evidence: linked focused unit suite passed 19/19 via pm test --run --progress --only-index 5 --timeout 600; compatibility/standalone SDK-hint checks passed 4/4; snapshot revert proof retained both failing mutants and fixed 2/2. New recovery proof has nine failing mutants and fixed 7/7. Typecheck, test compilation, whitespace checks and 116-declaration docstrings passed. One artifact was verified byte-for-byte against all nine current shipped files and passed all five layouts on both 2026.10.24 and 2026.10.28: 310 feature checks, 60 ordinary-writer interleavings, 50 compensated identities restored, 710 read-only provider requests and zero remote mutations. SHA-256 e18fca6bc1f7b00f1fda9a5613d3ce952adcde43a998304b6240336af2fb49a5. Both import aliases replay fresh input and preserve prior declared mappings; JSON/TOON and SDK-normalized export references agree. Existing read-only public-copy receipt remains 112 items, 232 files, 1644154 bytes, two inspections, unchanged source and 275-byte JSON; zero native unit contracts in that corpus is explicitly retained as a limitation. SDK development pin remains 2026.10.24; only the public peer/manifest/lock minimum changed to match required capabilities. No additional inline review findings were returned. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun gates and complete seeded models will run in exact-head CI, with final URLs/counts on PR 189. Release the claim for orchestrator verification; retain in_progress status. The SDK final-read-to-write window remains documented under pm-cli#1620, and the provider-less legacy replay follow-up is unchanged."
  "2026-10-29T10:26:46.875Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 CI cutoff reached after the required maximum 30-minute wait. Code head 0a6227f96d29aa50a4063c2d4a418e01f9cf8ce0: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40853593983 . The npm release gate and Node 22 test job each passed 432/432 tests, zero failures and zero skips; index.ts coverage is 99.66 percent lines, 96.87 percent branches and 100 percent functions at unchanged thresholds. Bun release gate and Node 26 remain queued with no result. This pending-evidence-only tracker commit changes no source or shipped artifact; its own exact-head CI remains pending and prior code-head results are not claimed for it. PR 189 remains ready for review, with verification pending in the orchestrator pipeline. Claim already released; feature remains in progress. Remaining ordinary-writer read-to-write window and provider-less legacy replay follow-up remain documented."
  "2026-10-29T10:39:13.667Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 resumed from clean 75acc52; origin/main is an ancestor, so no merge is needed. Both supplied blockers violate SDK mutation composition: native update can append separate field and closure events, and resubmitting an unchanged closed status can fail after fields are already saved. Per the fleet design directive, replace multi-item rollback and history ownership proofs with forward-only per-item imports, changed-field-only writes, immediate SDK revision/base checks, typed import_conflict skips and truthful applied/skipped reporting. Audit all legacy/unit-aware SDK and CLI aliases, previews, JSON/TOON and packed consumers; retain previous model coverage and add seeded failure/interleaving regressions plus disposable revert proof. Document remaining SDK precondition and ordinary-writer window (#1576/#1620)."
  "2026-10-29T10:52:02.772Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 class fix removes both production rollback coordinators, restoration/deletion receipts and history ownership verification. Legacy, unit-aware and estimate-ignore imports share one forward-only SDK coordinator. Updates compare SDK-canonical values, omit unchanged status/fields, validate a native close-route plan in an isolated SDK preview and re-read the paired revision immediately before apply. Every target has an exact typed result; earlier successes survive later failures, observer failures report applied state, and SDK graph ordering/hierarchy prerequisites propagate skips. The atomic flag and old importLinearAtomic name are deprecated forward-only compatibility surfaces. Superseded rollback assertions are migrated to the explicitly directed forward-only contract while retaining their history, retry, malformed-record, native-ID, custom-role and peer schedules; test coverage thresholds and original 500-sequence models are unchanged. No stronger guarantee than #1576/#1620 permits is claimed; arbitrary failures inside a native SDK close remain an explicit boundary."
  "2026-10-29T11:00:32.861Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: node test/revert-forward-import.ts docs/forward-import-revert.json passed. Four independent disposable mutants each failed 0 pass/1 fail: resubmit unchanged status/repeat closure; rollback earlier completed writes after a later failure; ignore a skipped prerequisite; omit the dependent-write revision fence. Fixed source passed 3/3. The reviewed checkout was never mutated by the reverts. Focused migrated unit suite passed 19/19, and six targeted close/dependency/preview/custom-terminal compatibility regressions passed 6/6. The new seeded 500 multi-item model also replays the independent SDK reference on retry, covering SDK close-assignee clearing and a final zero-write fixed point."
  "2026-10-29T11:11:32.185Z",codex-agent,"The new model identified terminal-assignee replay churn, beyond the two supplied blockers. Fixed by retaining the SDK primary close/cancel assignee-release result across imports, selected through registry roles rather than status names. Independent reference models execute SDK lifecycle producers; no hand-written normalization oracle is used. Short regressions verify terminal creation and repeated zero-write replays. Full 500-case multi-item fault schedules and both existing 500-sequence models remain in exact-head CI, per the saturated-host instruction; interrupted long local diagnostics are not counted as passes. Per-item receipts also include filtered/ambiguous provider identities and distinguish unconfirmed native-call outcomes after SDK readback, never claiming a changed target was untouched."
  "2026-10-29T11:36:16.170Z",codex-agent,"Packed minimum-host acceptance found an additional class instance: the SDK native preview correctly rejects symbolic links, while an installed package includes a runtime-only host SDK pointer under its extension directory. Raw preview therefore refused a completed-item edit despite local plain-tracker success. The close preflight now uses the existing guarded observational mirror, which omits that known code pointer without following it, then invokes the SDK preview on regular tracker data. All import aliases share this path. The completed-title/failure regression includes the installed-link shape and no git executable, and a fifth behavioral mutant removes the mirror to prove this boundary. The disposable 21-case model diagnostic passed all assertions with the committed 500-case model unchanged; full model evidence remains assigned to CI. Final linked unit run passed 19/19 via pm test, exit 0."
